Hey all,

I am trying to use unmarked to calculate bird densities from line transect data collected before and during a cull in four regions (BACI). My aim it to asses if the target species densities decreased, and if any corresponding changes in native species were seen. Surveys were conducted at 8 transects (treatment area) and 4 transects (control area) twice a month for 5 months before an invasive species cull (10 repeats). During the cull, surveys were conducted

once a month at the same transects for 12 months (12 repeats). All birds seen or heard within the 50m (each way) strip width on a 1000m transect were recorded (100,000m2).

I am having trouble understanding how to format the data frame to analyze the data using gdistsamp. I have already successfully ran the data using distsamp, but models had poor fit (very few records at 0m on the transect). I am after an example data frame showing how you would set up the formatting of a data frame for a multi-survey, multi species approach. Currently i am running into errors using gdistamp and i know it is related to the data frame being set up incorrectly.

If someone has their own code and a few rows of data they would be willing to share that would be amazing.

